exports[`markdown export coverage renders the kitchen-sink spec: api thing-created 1`] = `
"# Thing created

Webhook: the API sends this request to you.

Operation ID: \`thingCreated\`

OpenAPI specification: /kitchen-sink.yaml

## Request body

### Content type: \`application/json\`

Schema: \`object\`

A thing

More information: https://example.com/schemas/thing

- \`id\` (string, read-only)
- \`name\` (string, required, min length: 1, max length: 64, examples: \`Widget\`, \`Sprocket\`)
- \`kind\` (string, required, discriminator)
  - The value selects one of these schemas:
    - \`gadget\`: Gadget (object)
      - \`batteries\` (integer, >= 1)
    - \`gizmo\`: Gizmo (object)
      - \`gears\` (any of)
        - One or more of these options:
          - Option 1 (integer)
          - Option 2 (string, pattern: \`^[0-9]+$\`)
- \`size\` (integer | null, nullable, > 0, multiple of 5)
- \`coordinates\` (array, min items: 2, max items: 2)
  - \`coordinates[0]\` (number, item 1)
    Latitude
  - \`coordinates[1]\` (number, item 2)
    Longitude
- \`labels\` (object, property names: pattern: \`^[a-z-]+$\`)
  - \`labels.<key matching ^x->\` (string, pattern property)
- \`notThis\` (any, must not be: string)
- \`shipping\` (object, \`postalCode\` requires \`country\`)
  - \`shipping.country\` (string)
  - \`shipping.postalCode\` (string)
  - Conditional rule:
    - If the value matches:
      - \`shipping.country\` (constant, value: \`US\`)
    - Then it must also match:
      - \`shipping.postalCode\` (any, pattern: \`^[0-9]{5}$\`)
    - Otherwise it must match:
      - \`shipping.postalCode\` (any, pattern: \`^[A-Z0-9 ]+$\`)
- \`status\` (string, possible values: \`active\`, \`retired\`, default: \`active\`)
  - \`active\`: In use
  - \`retired\`: No longer in use
- \`owner\` (circular reference to Thing)
- \`longNote\` (string)
  Example:

  \`\`\`
  This example is intentionally long so that it is longer than the inline example limit of one hundred twenty characters, so it is shown as a separate code block.
  \`\`\`

- \`x-internal\` (string)

## Responses

### 200

Webhook received
"
`;

exports[`markdown export coverage renders the kitchen-sink spec: api update-thing 1`] = `
"# Update a thing

\`PUT /things/{thingId}\`

Operation ID: \`updateThing\`

Tags: \`things\`

OpenAPI specification: /kitchen-sink.yaml

More information: Update guide https://example.com/docs/update-thing

> **Deprecated.** Use PATCH instead.

Replaces a thing.

## Servers

- \`https://api.example.com/{region}\`: Regional server
  - Variable \`region\` (default: \`us\`, possible values: \`us\`, \`eu\`): Deployment region

## Authentication

Use one of these options:

- \`apiKey\` (API key in header \`X-API-Key\`)
- \`oauth\` (OAuth 2.0: clientCredentials (token URL https://example.com/oauth/token), scopes: \`things:write\`)

## Parameters

### Path parameters

- \`thingId\` (string<uuid>, required)
  Thing ID

### Query parameters

- \`filter\` (object, style: deepObject, explode: true)
  - \`filter.color\` (string)
- \`tags\` (string[], style: pipeDelimited, explode: false, possible item values: \`red\`, \`green\`)

### Header parameters

- \`X-Trace\` (string, deprecated)
  Example \`short\`: \`abc\`

### Cookie parameters

- \`session\` (string)

## Request body (required)

The new thing

### Content type: \`application/json\`

Schema: \`object\`

A thing

More information: https://example.com/schemas/thing

- \`id\` (string, read-only)
- \`name\` (string, required, min length: 1, max length: 64, examples: \`Widget\`, \`Sprocket\`)
- \`kind\` (string, required, discriminator)
  - The value selects one of these schemas:
    - \`gadget\`: Gadget (object)
      - \`batteries\` (integer, >= 1)
    - \`gizmo\`: Gizmo (object)
      - \`gears\` (any of)
        - One or more of these options:
          - Option 1 (integer)
          - Option 2 (string, pattern: \`^[0-9]+$\`)
- \`size\` (integer | null, nullable, > 0, multiple of 5)
- \`coordinates\` (array, min items: 2, max items: 2)
  - \`coordinates[0]\` (number, item 1)
    Latitude
  - \`coordinates[1]\` (number, item 2)
    Longitude
- \`labels\` (object, property names: pattern: \`^[a-z-]+$\`)
  - \`labels.<key matching ^x->\` (string, pattern property)
- \`notThis\` (any, must not be: string)
- \`shipping\` (object, \`postalCode\` requires \`country\`)
  - \`shipping.country\` (string)
  - \`shipping.postalCode\` (string)
  - Conditional rule:
    - If the value matches:
      - \`shipping.country\` (constant, value: \`US\`)
    - Then it must also match:
      - \`shipping.postalCode\` (any, pattern: \`^[0-9]{5}$\`)
    - Otherwise it must match:
      - \`shipping.postalCode\` (any, pattern: \`^[A-Z0-9 ]+$\`)
- \`status\` (string, possible values: \`active\`, \`retired\`, default: \`active\`)
  - \`active\`: In use
  - \`retired\`: No longer in use
- \`owner\` (circular reference to Thing)
- \`longNote\` (string)
  Example:

  \`\`\`
  This example is intentionally long so that it is longer than the inline example limit of one hundred twenty characters, so it is shown as a separate code block.
  \`\`\`

- \`x-internal\` (string)

Example \`basic (A basic thing)\`:

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"name\\": \\"Widget\\",
  \\"kind\\": \\"gadget\\"
}
\`\`\`

### Content type: \`multipart/form-data\`

Schema: \`object\`

- \`file\` (string, media type: \`image/png\`, encoding: \`base64\`)
- \`meta\` (object)
  - \`meta.label\` (string)

Encoding of each part:

- \`file\`: content type \`image/png, image/jpeg\`
  Headers:
  - \`X-Rate-Limit\` (integer)
- \`meta\`: content type \`application/json\`

## Responses

### 200

Updated thing

Response headers:

- \`ETag\` (string)
  Version tag

#### Content type: \`application/json\`

Schema: \`object\`

A thing

More information: https://example.com/schemas/thing

- \`id\` (string, read-only)
- \`name\` (string, required, min length: 1, max length: 64, examples: \`Widget\`, \`Sprocket\`)
- \`kind\` (string, required, discriminator)
  - The value selects one of these schemas:
    - \`gadget\`: Gadget (object)
      - \`batteries\` (integer, >= 1)
    - \`gizmo\`: Gizmo (object)
      - \`gears\` (any of)
        - One or more of these options:
          - Option 1 (integer)
          - Option 2 (string, pattern: \`^[0-9]+$\`)
- \`size\` (integer | null, nullable, > 0, multiple of 5)
- \`coordinates\` (array, min items: 2, max items: 2)
  - \`coordinates[0]\` (number, item 1)
    Latitude
  - \`coordinates[1]\` (number, item 2)
    Longitude
- \`labels\` (object, property names: pattern: \`^[a-z-]+$\`)
  - \`labels.<key matching ^x->\` (string, pattern property)
- \`notThis\` (any, must not be: string)
- \`shipping\` (object, \`postalCode\` requires \`country\`)
  - \`shipping.country\` (string)
  - \`shipping.postalCode\` (string)
  - Conditional rule:
    - If the value matches:
      - \`shipping.country\` (constant, value: \`US\`)
    - Then it must also match:
      - \`shipping.postalCode\` (any, pattern: \`^[0-9]{5}$\`)
    - Otherwise it must match:
      - \`shipping.postalCode\` (any, pattern: \`^[A-Z0-9 ]+$\`)
- \`status\` (string, possible values: \`active\`, \`retired\`, default: \`active\`)
  - \`active\`: In use
  - \`retired\`: No longer in use
- \`owner\` (circular reference to Thing)
- \`longNote\` (string)
  Example:

  \`\`\`
  This example is intentionally long so that it is longer than the inline example limit of one hundred twenty characters, so it is shown as a separate code block.
  \`\`\`

- \`x-internal\` (string)

Links:

- \`GetThing\`: operation \`getThing\`. Fetch the updated thing
  - Parameter \`thingId\`: \`$response.body#/id\`

### 4XX

Client error

#### Content type: \`application/problem+json\`

Schema: \`object\`

Problem

- \`type\` (string<uri>)
- \`detail\` (string)

## Callbacks

### Callback \`thingChanged\`: \`POST {$request.body#/callbackUrl}\`

Thing changed

#### Request body

##### Content type: \`application/json\`

Schema: \`object\`

- \`eventId\` (string)
- \`changedFields\` (string[])

#### Responses

##### 204

Callback received
"
`;

exports[`markdown export coverage renders the kitchen-sink spec: info kitchen-sink 1`] = `
"# Kitchen Sink

Version: \`1.0.0\`

OpenAPI specification: /kitchen-sink.yaml

Uses every OpenAPI feature the markdown export must cover.

## Authentication

- \`apiKey\`: API key in header \`X-API-Key\`
- \`oauth\`: OAuth 2.0: clientCredentials (token URL https://example.com/oauth/token)

## Operations

- [Update a thing](/docs/kitchen-sink/update-thing.md): \`PUT /things/{thingId}\`
- [Thing created](/docs/kitchen-sink/thing-created.md): \`EVENT webhook\`
"
`;

